 | 0253 | 2026-11-18 | Alloys phase P4a: the app-side plumbing that reaches an Alloy. **Nothing in the app calls it yet**, so it changes no behaviour (P5 moves the callers over one Element per patch). New `src/alloyhost/ctx.ts` builds the `Ctx` an Alloy is given: each Alloy sees only its own secrets and settings, and one `http.json` helper treats a network failure or 5xx as a retryable `AlloyNetworkError` and a 4xx as an `AlloyUserError`. New `src/alloyhost/store.ts` is an in-memory `LocalStore` (the persistent one for Pure Tillium is P7). New `src/alloyhost/router.ts`: `createRouter` looks up the Alloy selected for an Element and returns its functions with the Ctx already applied (`api`, `need`, `has(element, fn)` for optional features, `missingRequired`). An install that never chose reads as today's behaviour (`legacySelection`); a saved choice of an unknown Alloy, one that cannot do the Element, or one the build policy removed reads as Off rather than crashing. In practice mode the write functions (`createItem`, `adjust`, `record`, `refund`, `debit` and so on, listed per Element in `WRITES`) refuse with `PracticeBlockedError` before reaching the Alloy, and reads still run. 12 new tests in `tests/alloyrouter.test.ts`. P4b (the Shopify, Zeller and iCloud `alloy.ts` adapters and the registry entries) is next. |
 | 0254 | 2026-11-18 | Alloys phase P4b: the Shopify, Zeller and iCloud Alloys, as adapters over the code that is already there. **Nothing in the app calls them yet**, so behaviour is unchanged (P5 moves the callers over, one Element per patch). `src/alloys/shopify/alloy.ts` presents catalogue, stock, discounts, customers, orders, gift cards and shared state through the Element contracts; Shopify's own errors become the two Alloy errors (anything else, such as practice mode, passes through); the location comes from the Alloy's settings; `connect` lists the locations and names which Elements lack permissions; `changesSince` stamps its cursor before the call as the poll does today. `src/alloys/zeller/alloy.ts` is the card terminal over the existing `TerminalLike`, with the native reader code loaded only when asked for. `src/alloys/icloud.ts` is shared state over CloudKit (no iCloud Customers Element is built yet; the policy switch for it already exists). `src/alloys/index.ts` now registers all three. Four small fixes to the contract where the real functions carry more than the first draft showed: creating an item returns its three ids, updating one takes the product id too, refunds are per way paid with an optional restock flag, and gift cards have once-only debit and credit. `ELEMENT_FUNCTIONS` in `alloykit/elements.ts` lists the required and optional functions of each Element, and the new `tests/alloyconformance.test.ts` holds every registered Alloy to it, then runs the Shopify Alloy against the fake Shopify (19 tests). The `pendingEntry` boundary exception is gone; the other `TRANSITION` exceptions stay until P5. Full suite 2124 passing. |
 | 0255 | 2026-11-18 | Alloys phase P5a: the first caller moves onto the router, **Discounts**. The import and the half-hourly refresh in `sync.ts` used to call Shopify for automatic discounts and manual presets themselves; they now call `loadDiscounts()` (new `src/alloyhost/discounts.ts`), which asks the router for the Discounts Element. With the legacy default selection that is the Shopify Alloy while a Shopify login exists, which makes the same two calls in the same order, so nothing changes for you. If the Element is off, or there is no login (or practice mode, which reads as no login), discounts read as empty and nothing is sent. New `src/alloyhost/appRouter.ts` is the one router the app uses: built from the registry, reading the live location and login each time, with the selection fixed at the legacy default until the picker (P6) saves a choice. 5 new tests in `tests/alloyp5discounts.test.ts` pin that the router result equals calling Shopify directly, the call order, the empty cases, and that `sync.ts` has no direct discount calls left. Full suite 2129 passing. |
+| 0256 | 2026-11-18 | Alloys phase P5b: **Customers** moves onto the router. The Customers screen (search, create, edit) and the customer sheet in the cart (remote search, create) no longer import the Shopify customer file; they ask for the function through `needFeature('customers', ...)` (new `src/alloyhost/need.ts`). With the legacy default that reaches the same Shopify calls with the same inputs, and the screens show the same words when Shopify is not there: the old "Shopify is not set up - open More ▸ Settings ▸ Shopify." without a login, and the old practice-mode message in practice. Once a person has chosen their own setup, the message names the Element instead, and an Alloy that lacks a function (say, no "edit customer") gives a plain "cannot do that" error. One contract change: the customer input carries first and last name separately, as the till asks for them, rather than one name that the Alloy would have to split. The practice-mode branches in the screens are untouched. 5 new tests in `tests/alloyp5customers.test.ts`; full suite 2134 passing. |
 | 0241 | 2026-11-14 | **B7e, Help pictures for three more pages (your request).** The picture engine (`src/lib/helpFigures.ts`) already drew 12 pages; this adds seven figures drawn from the real screens' labels: Cloud sync (set up, invite link, join, Back up everything and Export all events, which the page did not describe at all), Offline and sync errors (the Support & diagnostics Sync rows, with the new **Last full sync** line explained) and Split and part payments (the Split amount sheet and the Payment screen after a split). 15 of 68 pages now have a figure. No code; `help.json` rebuilt, the 63 help tests pass. Not looked at on a device: the pictures follow the screens' labels but I cannot see the iPad. The other 53 pages are not drawn; the Daily float report is the hardest (it draws notes and coins) and was left. | B7e |
 | 0240 | 2026-11-14 | **B8, review of the gift-card calls before the live test (your request).** Read `giftcards.ts` against Shopify's `giftCardCredit` and `giftCardDebit` pages: the mutations, fields and the `write_gift_card_transactions` scope are as documented. Shopify gives neither call an idempotency key, and the cancel side already looked in the card's history before crediting again, but the **charge did not**: if Shopify took the charge and the reply was lost, the app said "could not be charged", the cashier tapped again and the card was charged twice. New `debitGiftCardOnce` and `src/lib/shopify/giftCardOnce.ts`: the Nth payment of a sale has the same note on every retry (`POS sale <8 chars> tender N`), the card's history is read for it first, and a debit already there is not sent again (Shopify returns a debit as a negative amount, so amounts are compared by size). The credit side now uses the same helper. Pay.tsx charges through it. `tests/giftcardonce.test.ts` (6 tests) pass. DEVICE_TESTS T10 gains the Wi-Fi-off charge test and a check of the notes. **The live run is still yours:** it spends real gift-card value on your store. | B8 |
